<!--
	A deep INLINE container's prose run packs greedily and pairwise to <=100, exactly as
	in a block container: an element joins the line while it fits, and each break lands
	at the latest whitespace boundary that holds the limit.
-->
<div>
	<div>
		<div>
			<div>
				<div>
					<div>
						<span>
							dispatch on duplicate declaration names: <code>throw</code> | <code>warn</code>
							(default: emit <code>fallback</code> diagnostic, no dispatch)
						</span>
						<span>
							mid-run text packs onto the first element up to: <code>throw</code> (default: emit
							<code>fallback</code> diagnostic, no dispatch)
						</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
